{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M2tuuRTQyYkBpUVS2UiuaA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Runtime v0.1 verification record\n2\t\n3\tThe qualified route is a trusted local macOS runner using Temporal1.9.1 and existing\n4\tCodex/Claude subscriptions. Two useful accepted development tasks completed through\n5\tthe same DevelopmentTask, frozen acceptance, independent review and protected\n6\tPublisher. Runtime code is integrated through PR11; both useful outputs through\n7\tPR7 and PR12. Final documentation/evidence integration and the fresh Claude\n8\tcontinuity check are the remaining release checks at this document's draft revision.\n9\t\n10\t## Mandate §1 evidence\n11\t\n12\t| Capability | Observed evidence and scope |\n13\t|---|---|\n14\t| Autonomous completion | [Report task](../evidence/accepted-task/result.md): native sequencing through actual implementation, tests, independent review and automatic PR12 integration. [Evidence integrity task](../evidence/runs/runtime-evidence-index-1/result.md): same path, automatic PR7. |\n15\t| Persistent continuity | Shared AGENTS.md and living plan; [fresh Codex root/subdirectory probes](../evidence/startup/codex-root-0155/run.json), [Claude native root/subdirectory loading](../evidence/claude-qualification/result.md). Fresh final Claude developer-context audit is recorded separately before release. |\n16\t| Replaceable execution | [Actual native history proof](../evidence/accepted-task/continuity-proof.json): retained Codex1 interruption/Codex2 work → Claude3 → Codex4; old20 events unchanged inside final49; original workspace retained and source hashes checked. |\n17\t| Interruption/capacity | [Real model interruption](../evidence/accepted-task/attempt-1/result.json); [abrupt worker fixture](../evidence/recovery-probe/result.md) with actual native workflow/guardian/sandbox, old-writer refusal, deadline cleanup and explicit attempt2; supplied-known-quota wait survives restart with zero calls. Actual403 and deliberate wait retained; no actual quota exhaustion claim. |\n18\t| Controlled integration | PR7/12 exact candidate/test/review binding and server readback. [Negative connected fixtures](../evidence/connected-workflow/result.md) reject failed/missing/stale/self review and failed tests; ambiguous publication fixture reconciles once. [Live protection evidence](../evidence/integration/) retains missing/stale-check denials. Candidate cannot write host requirements or publish. |\n19\t| Repeatable useful use | Two accepted tasks on the same engine/activities/Publisher, with provider adapter added without replacing the engine. [Fresh restarts](../evidence/v0.1/restart-and-state.json) preserve report4/evidence1 attempts and one publication each, no new provider calls. Both delivered CLIs were used on actual project evidence. |\n20\t\n21\tFixture assertions, raw measurements and reviewer judgment remain distinct. Passing\n22\tone phase never published the unfinished report. Tests/review used candidate\n23\tf86a85c27d7cb2567d3c600292f213fa45067b7a, integrated as98b92a72da2671c0a517f674f8b023667c070bcb.\n24\tThe second task candidate38ecdaf7f989ab547740e23345c9cfbf8f69513c integrated as0fba283d5c6e19f30c9703eec88e6ea879435c16.\n25\tEvidence task completed while Claude access was deferred; D017 explains that bounded\n26\treordering. Both are now complete, using the same underlying route.\n27\t\n28\t## Actual use, coordination and resources\n29\t\n30\tCustomer Zero was Runtime's own project/development work: reporting JSONL execution\n31\tstatus/usage and verifying evidence file manifests. Both are standard-library CLIs,\n32\tnot extra demonstration documents. Behavioral contracts, isolated examples and\n33\tregression tests fit these bounded code tasks; native replay/negative fixtures\n34\tqualified the uncertain engine transitions. Symphony was evaluated first, then\n35\trejected for durability/provider-boundary needs (D011/D012); no replacement generic\n36\tscheduler was built. Temporal supplies durable history, signals and activity state.\n37\t\n38\tThe chain driver created/reviewed accepted inputs and corrected concrete supporting\n39\tdefects. Owner decisions concerned repository visibility and existing access; the\n40\towner did not relay prompts between executors. After the report continuation signal,\n41\tRuntime performed both executor steps, test gates, independent review and protected\n42\tmerge. The evidence task needed one submission. Actual coordination, all measured\n43\tprovider usage and unknown monetary/chain-driver totals are detailed in the two\n44\tlinked task reports. No new subscription, API billing or external permission was\n45\tintroduced. Per-call bounds are operational safeguards, not an invented project cap.\n46\t\n47\t## Start, resume and hand over\n48\t\n49\tUse [the runbook](runbook.md) for the exact local environment and commands. Begin with\n50\t[the plan](plan.md), inspect Git and recorded process identities, and confirm old\n51\twriters stopped. Both existing tasks are completed: `--resume` inspects them;\n52\tresubmission and access-restored signals are inappropriate. Do not delete state to\n53\tmake submission succeed. New work requires its own accepted task/brief and separately\n54\treviewed host verifier before Runtime starts implementation.\n55\t\n56\tThe final compressed native database and integrity hashes are in\n57\t[evidence/v0.1](../evidence/v0.1/). Local .runtime task directories retain frozen input,\n58\told/current candidate and immutable Git candidates. Source, candidate bundles,\n59\traw events, acceptance/review receipts and task histories are preserved in Git.\n60\tCredentials are intentionally absent. A fresh session on this workstation can\n61\tcontinue from the project; restoring another workstation also requires its own\n62\tqualified subscriptions, binaries and careful reconstruction from saved artifacts.\n63\tThis release does not claim a tested one-command disaster restore to another host.\n64\t\n65\t## Limits of the qualified route\n66\t\n67\t- Trusted single local Mac (macOS26.3 arm64), loopback development Temporal, one worker\n68\t  activity at a time. No production deployment, cloud service or multi-user isolation.\n69\t- Explicit regular tools/ source files in Nortropic/nortropic-runtime; no arbitrary\n70\t  repository/language or general hostile-host guarantee. Claude only has native\n71\t  Read/Edit/Write; Codex/test/reviewer execution uses the qualified native sandbox.\n72\t- Bound process groups and abrupt worker death were tested. Arbitrary guardian\n73\t  SIGKILL, deliberately detached hostile descendants and host compromise were not.\n74\t- Known supplied capacity/access waits persist. Automatic weekly quota discovery\n75\t  and actual vendor quota exhaustion were not tested; failures never trigger blind\n76\t  automatic model retries. Review rejection waits for operator diagnosis rather than\n77\t  an automatic repair loop. Ambiguous publication requires inspected reconciliation.\n78\t- GitHub required contexts/strict base/admin/linear protection are active. This plan\n79\t  accepts status writers from any app; host publication credential isolation matters.\n80\t- Report status is deliberately conservative about failed tool items and is distinct\n81\t  from candidate/task acceptance. Reported token/cache/list-price fields are retained;\n82\t  subscription monetary attribution and root-session total usage are unknown.\n83\t- v0.1 covers these tasks and conditions. Further business features or continuous\n84\t  self-improvement require another applicable accepted task.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7ea7a62-668d-4328-ab22-c88d5a0db694","uuid":"7d3990ed-a5f7-4c65-8d09-11fe0d6bfa36","timestamp":"2026-09-19T12:46:34.060Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/elinhaggstrom/Nortropic Runtime/docs/runtime-v0.1.md","content":"# Runtime v0.1 verification record\n\nThe qualified route is a trusted local macOS runner using Temporal1.9.1 and existing\nCodex/Claude subscriptions. Two useful accepted development tasks completed through\nthe same DevelopmentTask, frozen acceptance, independent review and protected\nPublisher. Runtime code is integrated through PR11; both useful outputs through\nPR7 and PR12. Final documentation/evidence integration and the fresh Claude\ncontinuity check are the remaining release checks at this document's draft revision.\n\n## Mandate §1 evidence\n\n| Capability | Observed evidence and scope |\n|---|---|\n| Autonomous completion | [Report task](../evidence/accepted-task/result.md): native sequencing through actual implementation, tests, independent review and automatic PR12 integration. [Evidence integrity task](../evidence/runs/runtime-evidence-index-1/result.md): same path, automatic PR7. |\n| Persistent continuity | Shared AGENTS.md and living plan; [fresh Codex root/subdirectory probes](../evidence/startup/codex-root-0155/run.json), [Claude native root/subdirectory loading](../evidence/claude-qualification/result.md). Fresh final Claude developer-context audit is recorded separately before release. |\n| Replaceable execution | [Actual native history proof](../evidence/accepted-task/continuity-proof.json): retained Codex1 interruption/Codex2 work → Claude3 → Codex4; old20 events unchanged inside final49; original workspace retained and source hashes checked. |\n| Interruption/capacity | [Real model interruption](../evidence/accepted-task/attempt-1/result.json); [abrupt worker fixture](../evidence/recovery-probe/result.md) with actual native workflow/guardian/sandbox, old-writer refusal, deadline cleanup and explicit attempt2; supplied-known-quota wait survives restart with zero calls. Actual403 and deliberate wait retained; no actual quota exhaustion claim. |\n| Controlled integration | PR7/12 exact candidate/test/review binding and server readback. [Negative connected fixtures](../evidence/connected-workflow/result.md) reject failed/missing/stale/self review and failed tests; ambiguous publication fixture reconciles once. [Live protection evidence](../evidence/integration/) retains missing/stale-check denials. Candidate cannot write host requirements or publish. |\n| Repeatable useful use | Two accepted tasks on the same engine/activities/Publisher, with provider adapter added without replacing the engine. [Fresh restarts](../evidence/v0.1/restart-and-state.json) preserve report4/evidence1 attempts and one publication each, no new provider calls. Both delivered CLIs were used on actual project evidence. |\n\nFixture assertions, raw measurements and reviewer judgment remain distinct. Passing\none phase never published the unfinished report. Tests/review used candidate\nf86a85c27d7cb2567d3c600292f213fa45067b7a, integrated as98b92a72da2671c0a517f674f8b023667c070bcb.\nThe second task candidate38ecdaf7f989ab547740e23345c9cfbf8f69513c integrated as0fba283d5c6e19f30c9703eec88e6ea879435c16.\nEvidence task completed while Claude access was deferred; D017 explains that bounded\nreordering. Both are now complete, using the same underlying route.\n\n## Actual use, coordination and resources\n\nCustomer Zero was Runtime's own project/development work: reporting JSONL execution\nstatus/usage and verifying evidence file manifests. Both are standard-library CLIs,\nnot extra demonstration documents. Behavioral contracts, isolated examples and\nregression tests fit these bounded code tasks; native replay/negative fixtures\nqualified the uncertain engine transitions. Symphony was evaluated first, then\nrejected for durability/provider-boundary needs (D011/D012); no replacement generic\nscheduler was built. Temporal supplies durable history, signals and activity state.\n\nThe chain driver created/reviewed accepted inputs and corrected concrete supporting\ndefects. Owner decisions concerned repository visibility and existing access; the\nowner did not relay prompts between executors. After the report continuation signal,\nRuntime performed both executor steps, test gates, independent review and protected\nmerge. The evidence task needed one submission. Actual coordination, all measured\nprovider usage and unknown monetary/chain-driver totals are detailed in the two\nlinked task reports. No new subscription, API billing or external permission was\nintroduced. Per-call bounds are operational safeguards, not an invented project cap.\n\n## Start, resume and hand over\n\nUse [the runbook](runbook.md) for the exact local environment and commands. Begin with\n[the plan](plan.md), inspect Git and recorded process identities, and confirm old\nwriters stopped. Both existing tasks are completed: `--resume` inspects them;\nresubmission and access-restored signals are inappropriate. Do not delete state to\nmake submission succeed. New work requires its own accepted task/brief and separately\nreviewed host verifier before Runtime starts implementation.\n\nThe final compressed native database and integrity hashes are in\n[evidence/v0.1](../evidence/v0.1/). Local .runtime task directories retain frozen input,\nold/current candidate and immutable Git candidates. Source, candidate bundles,\nraw events, acceptance/review receipts and task histories are preserved in Git.\nCredentials are intentionally absent. A fresh session on this workstation can\ncontinue from the project; restoring another workstation also requires its own\nqualified subscriptions, binaries and careful reconstruction from saved artifacts.\nThis release does not claim a tested one-command disaster restore to another host.\n\n## Limits of the qualified route\n\n- Trusted single local Mac (macOS26.3 arm64), loopback development Temporal, one worker\n  activity at a time. No production deployment, cloud service or multi-user isolation.\n- Explicit regular tools/ source files in Nortropic/nortropic-runtime; no arbitrary\n  repository/language or general hostile-host guarantee. Claude only has native\n  Read/Edit/Write; Codex/test/reviewer execution uses the qualified native sandbox.\n- Bound process groups and abrupt worker death were tested. Arbitrary guardian\n  SIGKILL, deliberately detached hostile descendants and host compromise were not.\n- Known supplied capacity/access waits persist. Automatic weekly quota discovery\n  and actual vendor quota exhaustion were not tested; failures never trigger blind\n  automatic model retries. Review rejection waits for operator diagnosis rather than\n  an automatic repair loop. Ambiguous publication requires inspected reconciliation.\n- GitHub required contexts/strict base/admin/linear protection are active. This plan\n  accepts status writers from any app; host publication credential isolation matters.\n- Report status is deliberately conservative about failed tool items and is distinct\n  from candidate/task acceptance. Reported token/cache/list-price fields are retained;\n  subscription monetary attribution and root-session total usage are unknown.\n- v0.1 covers these tasks and conditions. Further business features or continuous\n  self-improvement require another applicable accepted task.\n","numLines":85,"startLine":1,"totalLines":85}}}
