{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ADNKeZv94FjUBuXxTJqMJz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Running the qualified local route\n2\t\n3\tThe living plan owns the current task, wait reason, attempt identity and next\n4\tspecific action. Read it before starting any process. Both accepted tasks are completed; see docs/runtime-v0.1.md for measured scope and limits.\n5\t\n6\tThe current installation uses a pinned local Temporal 1.9.1 development service,\n7\tPython 3.12 with temporalio1.33.0 in `.runtime/temporal-venv`, and Codex0.155.1\n8\tunder `.runtime/bin`. Dependency lock and recorded hashes are under config/ and\n9\tevidence/startup/. Authentication uses the already authorized Codex and Claude Max subscriptions;\n10\tGitHub authentication is available only to the host publication activity. No\n11\tTemporal Cloud or paid API fallback is configured. This is a trusted local Mac\n12\tinstallation, not a deployed multi-user service.\n13\t\n14\tA new accepted task must have committed task JSON and brief in tasks/ plus a\n15\treviewed host-owned acceptance module under acceptance/. Its digest, exact current\n16\tmain base and explicit allowed paths are fixed before implementation. The qualified\n17\troute supports the measured Codex-only and Codex→Claude→Codex tasks with regular\n18\tfiles under tools/. This is not qualification of arbitrary provider/task sequences.\n19\t\n20\t```sh\n21\t.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m runtime.run tasks/evidence-index.json\n22\t```\n23\t\n24\tThis starts one loopback Temporal service and one worker, submits the frozen task\n25\tonce, observes a bounded result, preserves history and stops service groups.\n26\tA completed existing task cannot be submitted again; existing task/evidence\n27\tfolders are never overwritten. The native SQLite database at\n28\t`.runtime/runtime.sqlite` is canonical engine state. Frozen input/candidate files\n29\tare under `.runtime/tasks/<id>`; durable evidence is under `evidence/runs/<id>`.\n30\tThe historical report task uses evidence/accepted-task/.\n31\t\n32\tInspect an existing run without resubmitting or buying access:\n33\t\n34\t```sh\n35\t.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m runtime.run tasks/evidence-index.json --resume\n36\t```\n37\t\n38\tExit0 means completed; exit1 can mean a deliberately preserved waiting state.\n39\tRead state.json and raw launch/result/acceptance/review artifacts before deciding\n40\twhat to do. Inspect recorded process identities/groups and verify old writers\n41\thave stopped. The CLI also refuses observed unfinished writers. A lost connection\n42\tis not proof that a provider has stopped. Never erase launch evidence or lock\n43\tfiles to bypass this check.\n44\t\n45\tAfter a concrete implementation diagnosis and materially changed prerequisite,\n46\tresume the SAME task with `--resume --diagnosis \"what changed and why\"`. This\n47\tsignals native history and increments the implementation attempt. There are no\n48\tautomatic model retries. The present route does not yet automate remediation of\n49\ta rejected review; it waits without publication.\n50\t\n51\tIf a publication response is ambiguous, first inspect remote PR/head/base and\n52\tpreserved local evidence. Then use `--resume --reconcile \"what was inspected\"`.\n53\tThe Publisher reconciles an already merged exact candidate before another remote\n54\tmutation; it rejects changed bases, heads, or inadequate receipts. Never post\n55\tsuccess statuses to bypass a failed or missing mandatory result.\n56\t\n57\tCandidate and reviewer have no publication tools, no network, and no host evidence\n58\twrite access. Reviewer source is read-only. A host creates exact Git objects,\n59\texecutes frozen acceptance in the native sandbox and binds both real run identities\n60\tbefore protected publication. Required branch statuses are exact-candidate checks;\n61\tthe current GitHub plan accepts status writers from any app, so host credential\n62\tisolation remains essential.\n63\t\n64\tNo general hostile detached-process or arbitrary-host-compromise guarantee is\n65\tclaimed. Per-invocation deadlines and process-group cleanup are measured local\n66\tsafeguards. See the evidence index and current limitations in docs/plan.md.\n67\t\n68\t### Restored Claude access on the retained report task\n69\t\n70\tThe qualified Claude path uses the existing Max subscription, pinned CLI2.1.257,\n71\tRead/Edit/Write only, exact accepted file grants, strict empty MCP and native\n72\tAGENTS.md file loading. Host runs tests after cleanup. A changed binary/auth path\n73\tstops before model invocation; diagnose/requalify rather than enabling API fallback.\n74\t\n75\tHistorical transition command (already completed; DO NOT run again for this task):\n76\tthe host generated, preserved and separately reviewed the same task's continuation\n77\ton clean integrated main, then invoked:\n78\t\n79\t```\n80\t.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m runtime.run tasks/run-report-continuation.json --resume --access-restored\n81\t```\n82\t\n83\tThis is for the existing waiting checkpoint only. It keeps the native workflow,\n84\told workspace, attempt counter and resource history. A second signal cannot repeat\n85\tan already-running step. Do not rerun preparation into partial state; inspect the\n86\tpreserved directories/receipt and native query before reconciling. After transition,\n87\tordinary observation uses the same input with `--resume` alone. Follow docs/plan.md\n88\tfor the actual current checkpoint; the command above is not a request to resubmit.\n89\t\n90\t### Selected dependencies and installation record\n91\t\n92\tThe current workstation is installed and qualified. Do not reinstall or update it\n93\tas part of ordinary resume. [dependencies.json](../evidence/v0.1/dependencies.json)\n94\trecords current binary hashes, Python3.12.13, macOS26.3 and arm64. Claude2.1.257's\n95\tbinary SHA256 is enforced by runtime/claude_profile.py; its native installed CLI\n96\tuses existing account credentials. A changed version/auth route requires a new\n97\tbounded qualification, never automatic API fallback.\n98\t\n99\tFor a fresh isolated project installation, inspect these exact selected artifacts\n100\tand their retained download/inspection records before extraction:\n101\t\n102\t- openai/codex release rust-v0.155.1: codex-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz and\n103\t  codex-code-mode-host-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz; extract only selected regular\n104\t  executables to .runtime/bin/codex-0.155.1 and .runtime/bin/codex-code-mode-host.\n105\t  Commands and outcomes: evidence/startup/codex-download/ and codex-host-download/.\n106\t- temporalio/cli release v1.9.1: temporal_cli_1.9.1_darwin_arm64.tar.gz; selected\n107\t  regular temporal member to .runtime/bin/temporal-1.9.1. Download and inspected\n108\t  archive hash/members: evidence/durable-probe/cli-download/ and cli-inspection.json.\n109\t- Python SDK and every transitive package/version/hash are fixed by\n110\t  config/temporal-probe-requirements.lock. The recorded installation used inspected\n111\t  wheels, no source build or extra startup .pth code (wheel-inspection.json).\n112\t\n113\tThe selected environment creation/install commands, for fresh paths only, are:\n114\t\n115\t```sh\n116\t/opt/homebrew/bin/python3.12 -m venv .runtime/temporal-venv\n117\t.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m pip download --only-binary=:all: --require-hashes -r config/temporal-probe-requirements.lock --dest .runtime/temporal-wheels\n118\t.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m pip install --no-index --find-links .runtime/temporal-wheels --require-hashes -r config/temporal-probe-requirements.lock\n119\t```\n120\t\n121\tNo Symphony dependency is used by the delivered runner; its historical probe\n122\tartifacts remain. Runtime starts pinned Temporal on loopback ports7339/7340/7341,\n123\tnamespace nortropic-runtime, task queue development, central SQLite and an exclusive\n124\tengine.lock. It stops service/worker groups after bounded observation. Never start\n125\tanother service while a recorded writer or listener is alive.\n126\t\n127\tRoutine support checks are `python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts -p \"test_*.py\" -v`\n128\tand `git diff --check`. Native replay runs without provider calls using\n129\t`.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m scripts.replay_runtime`. Historical experiment\n130\tscripts refuse their existing state/output paths; they are evidence reproductions,\n131\tnot restart commands. A new host restoration is not yet an end-to-end tested path.\n132\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7ea7a62-668d-4328-ab22-c88d5a0db694","uuid":"126f2058-bc06-49fb-85fb-ac8c727ac1d2","timestamp":"2026-09-19T12:46:53.842Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/elinhaggstrom/Nortropic Runtime/docs/runbook.md","content":"# Running the qualified local route\n\nThe living plan owns the current task, wait reason, attempt identity and next\nspecific action. Read it before starting any process. Both accepted tasks are completed; see docs/runtime-v0.1.md for measured scope and limits.\n\nThe current installation uses a pinned local Temporal 1.9.1 development service,\nPython 3.12 with temporalio1.33.0 in `.runtime/temporal-venv`, and Codex0.155.1\nunder `.runtime/bin`. Dependency lock and recorded hashes are under config/ and\nevidence/startup/. Authentication uses the already authorized Codex and Claude Max subscriptions;\nGitHub authentication is available only to the host publication activity. No\nTemporal Cloud or paid API fallback is configured. This is a trusted local Mac\ninstallation, not a deployed multi-user service.\n\nA new accepted task must have committed task JSON and brief in tasks/ plus a\nreviewed host-owned acceptance module under acceptance/. Its digest, exact current\nmain base and explicit allowed paths are fixed before implementation. The qualified\nroute supports the measured Codex-only and Codex→Claude→Codex tasks with regular\nfiles under tools/. This is not qualification of arbitrary provider/task sequences.\n\n```sh\n.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m runtime.run tasks/evidence-index.json\n```\n\nThis starts one loopback Temporal service and one worker, submits the frozen task\nonce, observes a bounded result, preserves history and stops service groups.\nA completed existing task cannot be submitted again; existing task/evidence\nfolders are never overwritten. The native SQLite database at\n`.runtime/runtime.sqlite` is canonical engine state. Frozen input/candidate files\nare under `.runtime/tasks/<id>`; durable evidence is under `evidence/runs/<id>`.\nThe historical report task uses evidence/accepted-task/.\n\nInspect an existing run without resubmitting or buying access:\n\n```sh\n.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m runtime.run tasks/evidence-index.json --resume\n```\n\nExit0 means completed; exit1 can mean a deliberately preserved waiting state.\nRead state.json and raw launch/result/acceptance/review artifacts before deciding\nwhat to do. Inspect recorded process identities/groups and verify old writers\nhave stopped. The CLI also refuses observed unfinished writers. A lost connection\nis not proof that a provider has stopped. Never erase launch evidence or lock\nfiles to bypass this check.\n\nAfter a concrete implementation diagnosis and materially changed prerequisite,\nresume the SAME task with `--resume --diagnosis \"what changed and why\"`. This\nsignals native history and increments the implementation attempt. There are no\nautomatic model retries. The present route does not yet automate remediation of\na rejected review; it waits without publication.\n\nIf a publication response is ambiguous, first inspect remote PR/head/base and\npreserved local evidence. Then use `--resume --reconcile \"what was inspected\"`.\nThe Publisher reconciles an already merged exact candidate before another remote\nmutation; it rejects changed bases, heads, or inadequate receipts. Never post\nsuccess statuses to bypass a failed or missing mandatory result.\n\nCandidate and reviewer have no publication tools, no network, and no host evidence\nwrite access. Reviewer source is read-only. A host creates exact Git objects,\nexecutes frozen acceptance in the native sandbox and binds both real run identities\nbefore protected publication. Required branch statuses are exact-candidate checks;\nthe current GitHub plan accepts status writers from any app, so host credential\nisolation remains essential.\n\nNo general hostile detached-process or arbitrary-host-compromise guarantee is\nclaimed. Per-invocation deadlines and process-group cleanup are measured local\nsafeguards. See the evidence index and current limitations in docs/plan.md.\n\n### Restored Claude access on the retained report task\n\nThe qualified Claude path uses the existing Max subscription, pinned CLI2.1.257,\nRead/Edit/Write only, exact accepted file grants, strict empty MCP and native\nAGENTS.md file loading. Host runs tests after cleanup. A changed binary/auth path\nstops before model invocation; diagnose/requalify rather than enabling API fallback.\n\nHistorical transition command (already completed; DO NOT run again for this task):\nthe host generated, preserved and separately reviewed the same task's continuation\non clean integrated main, then invoked:\n\n```\n.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m runtime.run tasks/run-report-continuation.json --resume --access-restored\n```\n\nThis is for the existing waiting checkpoint only. It keeps the native workflow,\nold workspace, attempt counter and resource history. A second signal cannot repeat\nan already-running step. Do not rerun preparation into partial state; inspect the\npreserved directories/receipt and native query before reconciling. After transition,\nordinary observation uses the same input with `--resume` alone. Follow docs/plan.md\nfor the actual current checkpoint; the command above is not a request to resubmit.\n\n### Selected dependencies and installation record\n\nThe current workstation is installed and qualified. Do not reinstall or update it\nas part of ordinary resume. [dependencies.json](../evidence/v0.1/dependencies.json)\nrecords current binary hashes, Python3.12.13, macOS26.3 and arm64. Claude2.1.257's\nbinary SHA256 is enforced by runtime/claude_profile.py; its native installed CLI\nuses existing account credentials. A changed version/auth route requires a new\nbounded qualification, never automatic API fallback.\n\nFor a fresh isolated project installation, inspect these exact selected artifacts\nand their retained download/inspection records before extraction:\n\n- openai/codex release rust-v0.155.1: codex-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz and\n  codex-code-mode-host-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz; extract only selected regular\n  executables to .runtime/bin/codex-0.155.1 and .runtime/bin/codex-code-mode-host.\n  Commands and outcomes: evidence/startup/codex-download/ and codex-host-download/.\n- temporalio/cli release v1.9.1: temporal_cli_1.9.1_darwin_arm64.tar.gz; selected\n  regular temporal member to .runtime/bin/temporal-1.9.1. Download and inspected\n  archive hash/members: evidence/durable-probe/cli-download/ and cli-inspection.json.\n- Python SDK and every transitive package/version/hash are fixed by\n  config/temporal-probe-requirements.lock. The recorded installation used inspected\n  wheels, no source build or extra startup .pth code (wheel-inspection.json).\n\nThe selected environment creation/install commands, for fresh paths only, are:\n\n```sh\n/opt/homebrew/bin/python3.12 -m venv .runtime/temporal-venv\n.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m pip download --only-binary=:all: --require-hashes -r config/temporal-probe-requirements.lock --dest .runtime/temporal-wheels\n.runtime/temporal-venv/bin/python -m pip install --no-index --find-links .runtime/temporal-wheels --require-hashes -r config/temporal-probe-requirements.lock\n```\n\nNo Symphony dependency